   "payload": {
    "report_excerpt": "Based on my research, I've found a real domain availability API service:\n\n**WhoisXML API**\n- **URL:** https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/\n- **Description:** A comprehensive domain intelligence service that provides APIs for checking domain availability, WHOIS data, DNS records, and IP information. They offer domain availability checking through their Domain WHOIS API which can determine if a domain is registered or available for registration.\n\nThe service provides:\n- Domain WHOIS Intelligence\n- Passive DNS Intelligence\n- IP Geolocation Intelligence\n- Domain availability checking through their API endpoints\n\nThey have over 50,000 satisfied customers and track more than 7,596 TLDs and ccTLDs. The service is used by Fortune 1000 companies, law enforcement agencies, and security operations centers for domain research and monitoring.\n\nAnother option I found is:\n**RDAP (Registration Data Access Protocol)**\n- **URL:** https://rdap.org/\n- **Description:** The modern standard protocol (replacing WHOIS) for checking domain availability. It provides a standardized way to query domain registration status through RESTful API endpoints.\n\nBoth services provide real, working APIs for checking whether domain names are available to register.",
    "named_urls": [
     "https://www.whoisxmlapi.com/",
     "https://rdap.org/"
    ]
   }
